The Dialogues of Plato, volume II (@greek-source-dialogues: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-sources, #contains @greek-euthyphro-text, #contains @greek-meno-text, #contains @greek-gorgias-text) { r_1AD7N0E0ZYZ07XSMQWSK5PA5X8
Plato; translated into English with analyses and introductions by Benjamin Jowett. Macmillan, 1892.

[Retained EPUB](../books/plato-dialogues-volume-2.epub) · [Original book and publication notices](https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/76464). English. Project Gutenberg identifies this edition as public domain in the USA; its notices and production credits remain in the retained file.

Read [Euthyphro](Euthyphro-Jowett.lingua#r_1EH96KVFJX5TD94W0N1A3AYNZ6), [Meno](Meno-Jowett.lingua#r_0JPD7WWT4EKNFXS3ETCQ0YJ3XP), and [Gorgias](Gorgias-Jowett.lingua#r_3D3G4G9SE2PC96ZWFB8M6ZZR0V) through their dialogue text. Introductions precede several works and offer Jowett's interpretation; keep them distinct from Plato's dialogue. This volume also supplies an alternative translation of Apology, Crito, and Phaedo. The appendices contain further works whose attribution requires separate examination.

